   ;; Upstream rewrites a heredoc end line into a SemiColon built without
   ;; source indices (its span reads back as [0 1] on any source) and rewrites
   ;; the text of the token after a semicolon-less end line (a `)` reads
   ;; "EOF\n;"). The patch keeps both tokens as the real source tokens: the
   ;; end line becomes a SemiColon over its own text and span, and the
   ;; following token keeps its own text, so every span is the source it
   ;; came from.
   :patches
   {"Java/PhpLexerBase.java"
    [["                            token = new CommonToken(PhpLexer.SemiColon, heredocIdentifier + \";\\n\");"
      "                            token.setType(PhpLexer.SemiColon);"]
     ["                            token.setText(heredocIdentifier + \"\\n;\");"
      "                            // keeps its own source text"]]},
